  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/FDCFF1">Definition <span data-tag="FDCFF1">5.5.8.18</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category which admits geometric realizations of simplicial objects. We will say that an object $P \in \calC $ is <em>projective</em> if the functor $\calC \rightarrow \SSet $ co-represented by $P$ commutes with geometric realizations.projective objectobject!projective </p>
